@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title hermes paradigm — general-purpose assistant, not a coding harness

' purpose: why hermes exists as a def, and why its Dockerfile/entrypoint break
'   from every other harness's shape
' covers: defs/hermes/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/hermes/entrypoint.sh
'
' ── WHY HERMES AND NOT xAI's "grok-bot" ─────────────────────────────────────
' This def was cut on a branch originally scoped for an xAI "grok-bot"
' integration. Research found neither xAI product fit: Grok Bot (the cloud
' teammate app) has no local binary at all — it runs on a shared cloud
' computer per account, isolation only between accounts, never between bots —
' so there is nothing for docker-sbx to sandbox. Grok Build (the CLI) has no
' documented sandbox or browser story. Hermes Agent (NousResearch, MIT)
' ships native browser automation (navigate/click/type/screenshot), takes any
' OpenAI-compatible endpoint, and already has a Docker backend — the actual
' shape a Cowork-style general assistant needs, which neither xAI product nor
' this repo's other candidate (Docker Agent, a bring-your-own-tools framework
' with no browser tool at all) provided out of the box.
'
' ── WHY NO Parent, UNLIKE EVERY OTHER DEF ───────────────────────────────────
' Every other harness here builds FROM proveo's own base chain
' (base/base-node/base-node-lsp/base-node-browser) and installs its CLI via
' npm/pypi on top. Hermes's own upstream image is a mature, actively
' maintained multi-stage build that already bakes Python, Node, a pinned
' Chromium, ffmpeg and ripgrep, supervised by s6-overlay. Re-deriving that on
' proveo's base — or worse, layering base-node-browser's OWN Chromium install
' on top of one already baked in — duplicates a large, fast-moving build this
' repo does not own, for no benefit over pinning the upstream tag directly.
' So `hermes`'s Spec in targets.go has no Parent/ParentOverride at all: it is
' `FROM nousresearch/hermes-agent:${HERMES_AGENT_VERSION}`, pinned by a plain
' EnvArg the same way codex pins `CODEX_VERSION`.
'
' ── WHY THE ENTRYPOINT OVERRIDES s6-overlay ─────────────────────────────────
' Upstream's own ENTRYPOINT runs s6-overlay's /init as PID 1, supervising a
' persistent stack: the main hermes process, a web dashboard, and per-profile
' gateway services that survive across sessions. That is the shape of a
' standing multi-tenant server, not this repo's model — every def here is one
' foreground agent process per ephemeral sandbox, launched by dumb-init +
' entrypoint.sh, torn down with the container. Keeping s6-overlay would mean
' this repo supervising services (the dashboard, gateways) nothing here ever
' needs, and reconciling "docker: sbx"'s ONE startup command against a
' multi-service supervision tree it was never designed for.
'
' So defs/hermes/Dockerfile overrides ENTRYPOINT to the usual
' `dumb-init -- /entrypoint.sh`. Because upstream's stage2-hook.sh (UID/GID
' remap, /opt/data volume ownership, config seeding, skills sync) normally
' runs as an s6 cont-init.d step before /init hands off, entrypoint.sh calls
' it directly, once, still as root — reusing upstream's own setup logic
' rather than reimplementing it, and the one reason this def stays root at
' build time when every other one here sets USER at build time. Root then
' drops to the "hermes" user through upstream's OWN exec shim
' (/opt/hermes/bin/hermes, which s6-setuidgid's into "hermes" when invoked as
' root), not a proveo-authored privilege drop.
'
actor "Operator" as OP

node "hermes container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "defs/hermes/entrypoint.sh\n(dumb-init PID 1)" as EP <<app>>
  component "stage2-hook.sh\n(upstream setup, run once)" as HOOK <<app>>
  component "/opt/hermes/bin/hermes\n(exec shim: root -> hermes user)" as SHIM <<app>>
  component "hermes chat / native browser tool" as CLI <<app>>
  database "/proveo-home/data (HERMES_HOME)" as HOME <<db>>
  database "/app — repo (rw, .git rw)" as WS <<db>>
}

cloud "Provider API\n(OpenAI-compatible endpoint)" as BACKEND
cloud "Ollama sidecar\n(PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL)" as OLLAMA

OP ARROW_MAIN EP : starts container
EP ARROW_MAIN HOOK : run once, as root
HOOK ARROW_MAIN HOME : remap uid, chown, seed config
EP ARROW_MAIN SHIM : exec
SHIM ARROW_MAIN CLI : drop to "hermes" user
CLI ARROW_MAIN WS : read/edit repo
CLI ARROW_OPTIONAL BACKEND : hosted key (OPENAI_API_KEY, etc.)
CLI ARROW_OPTIONAL OLLAMA : PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL set

note bottom of CLI
  **Real browser-profile reuse ships OFF by default.**
  Upstream can copy the operator's default browser
  profile — cookies, saved logins — into the sandbox.
  This def never turns that on for them.
end note

note bottom of SHIM
  **Bot-detection evasion is excluded on purpose.**
  Upstream's cloud tier offers residential proxies,
  CAPTCHA solving, and fingerprint randomization. None
  of it is wired into this def, ever — decided the same
  session Hermes was chosen, not an oversight.
end note

@enduml
